1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:04,254
<i>Things can't always be this way.</i>
<i>Especially now, Caloy!</i>

2
00:00:04,337 --> 00:00:06,214
<i>I can already imagine it.</i>

3
00:00:06,297 --> 00:00:08,967
<i>Her friends would invite me out.</i>

4
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:11,553
<i>"Hey, Abi! Let's have a drink."</i>

5
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:14,305
<i>Everything you said will happen.</i>

6
00:00:14,389 --> 00:00:15,974
<i>Well? Is it okay now?</i>

7
00:00:16,057 --> 00:00:17,434
<i>What is this?</i>

8
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:19,060
<i>"5:00 p.m."?</i>

9
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:21,312
<i>"At Le Jardin Hotel?"</i>

10
00:00:21,396 --> 00:00:23,356
<i>Why were you talking with Val?</i>

11
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,482
[YANI GRUNTS]

12
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:27,777
<i>I was asking her</i>
<i>to help me propose to you.</i>

13
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:30,405
- <i>Bye! Take care!</i>
- [PHONE RINGING]

14
00:00:31,781 --> 00:00:32,699
<i>Hello?</i>

15
00:00:32,782 --> 00:00:33,908
<i>Sweetie?</i>

16
00:00:33,992 --> 00:00:38,997
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

17
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:42,459
[MUSIC FADES]

18
00:00:53,178 --> 00:00:54,804
A sorry letter?

19
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:56,598
For Billy?

20
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:02,437
Oh, it's a song.

21
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,521
[PEN THUDS]

22
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:11,154
Are you still affected by what happened?

23
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:15,283
Yeah.

24
00:01:16,076 --> 00:01:18,161
This is my way of, like…

25
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:19,954
Expressing your guilt.

26
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:21,122
Something like that.

27
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:23,374
What about the promise you made to me?

28
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:27,420
You said you'd compose a song for me.

29
00:01:29,255 --> 00:01:31,883
Um… did you forget something?

30
00:01:33,551 --> 00:01:35,303
Ah…
[CHUCKLES]

31
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:38,932
I was just at the diner down the street.

32
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:42,644
It was too noisy here. I needed to think.

33
00:01:42,727 --> 00:01:43,812
Think about…?

34
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:46,022
Here.

35
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:49,150
[VALERIE] <i>Hi, Valerieverse fam.</i>

36
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:52,904
<i>This is me speaking up about</i>
<i>my ex's altercation incident.</i>

37
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:57,158
<i>As most of you guys know,</i>
<i>Jordan is a gentle soul.</i>

38
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:59,869
<i>But you also know</i>
<i>how protective he can be.</i>

39
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:02,413
<i>He will never hurt anyone unprovoked.</i>

40
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:07,085
<i>So this is me asking everyone</i>
<i>to stay respectful,</i>

41
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:08,878
<i>avoid spreading fake news,</i>

42
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:11,005
<i>and let the proper process unfold.</i>

43
00:02:11,089 --> 00:02:15,343
I have millions of followers
across all social media platforms.

44
00:02:15,426 --> 00:02:17,554
I can ask them to repost it.

45
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:22,058
Val… Wow. Thank you.

46
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:25,979
But… why are you doing this?

47
00:02:26,062 --> 00:02:27,480
Because I still…

48
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:31,693
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:34,112
I still am a part of LoveList.

50
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:37,407
And just like Billy,

51
00:02:38,575 --> 00:02:39,617
I love…

52
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:44,873
I love the company too.

53
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:46,708
Well, I can't thank you enough.

54
00:02:46,791 --> 00:02:50,253
I'm just doing my job as a consultant
and a content creator.

55
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:51,921
Well, you deserve a raise.

56
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:54,340
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

57
00:02:54,424 --> 00:02:55,341
[GASPS]

58
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:57,969
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:02:58,553 --> 00:02:59,679
Oliver?

60
00:02:59,762 --> 00:03:00,680
Oliver!

61
00:03:00,763 --> 00:03:01,639
No.

62
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:03,141
Don't go with him.

63
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:04,601
Don't.

64
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:05,852
Let's go.

65
00:03:05,935 --> 00:03:07,186
Don't go with him!

66
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:08,313
Oliver, no!

67
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:09,230
No!

68
00:03:09,314 --> 00:03:10,356
Oliver!

69
00:03:11,357 --> 00:03:12,358
Come on.

70
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:17,363
[GASPS, BREATHING SHAKILY]

71
00:03:17,447 --> 00:03:20,533
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]

72
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:21,910
[SIGHS]

73
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:28,124
[MUMBLES INAUDIBLY]

74
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:40,970
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

75
00:04:19,217 --> 00:04:20,343
Oliver?

76
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:24,681
[MAN ON VIDEO] <i>If you want</i>
<i>to throw killer punches,</i>

77
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:26,933
<i>you first need a firm stance.</i>

78
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:30,436
<i>Power starts from your feet,</i>
<i>not your fists.</i>

79
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:37,193
- [GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [OLIVER HUFFING]

80
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:38,987
Good morning!

81
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:42,907
You're up early.

82
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:44,742
What are you doing?

83
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:48,037
I'm practicing boxing so I'm ready
when Biboy bullies me again.

84
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:49,998
[WHOOSHING]

85
00:04:50,081 --> 00:04:52,917
Have you changed your patch?
Have you eaten yet?

86
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:54,877
Yes, Billy. I have everything
under control.

87
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:56,296
Okay.

88
00:04:56,379 --> 00:04:59,132
Remember, just use boxing
to defend yourself.

89
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:01,426
Don't go starting fights, okay?

90
00:05:01,509 --> 00:05:03,052
Wait, wait, wait.

91
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:04,429
I told you not to let it reach a point

92
00:05:04,512 --> 00:05:06,222
where you have to defend
yourself, remember?

93
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:08,141
Avoid any fight.

94
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:09,809
Well, I'm good at dodging punches.

95
00:05:09,892 --> 00:05:10,935
Look. I'll show you.

96
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:12,812
- Whoa.
- I'm good, right?

97
00:05:12,895 --> 00:05:14,397
That's amazing!

98
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:18,151
Oliver. Let's go somewhere?

99
00:05:18,234 --> 00:05:20,737
- Yeah. I'd like that.
- Okay.

100
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:23,865
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

101
00:05:25,366 --> 00:05:26,909
[JORDAN] Is it good, Grandpa?

102
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:30,621
It's a new addition to our menu.

103
00:05:30,705 --> 00:05:34,792
Well, beef salpicao isn't usually
eaten for breakfast.

104
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:37,420
[CHUCKLES] But it's good.

105
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:39,630
- Thank you.
- Oh.

106
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:42,050
Don't tell your mom about this, okay?

107
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:45,970
She doesn't like me eating
fatty or greasy foods.

108
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:49,891
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

109
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:51,142
Okay, Grandpa.

110
00:05:52,727 --> 00:05:54,020
It'll be our secret.

111
00:05:54,103 --> 00:05:55,605
[JUDE LAUGHING]

112
00:05:56,272 --> 00:05:57,398
[JUDE] Okay.

113
00:05:57,899 --> 00:06:02,904
[MUSIC BECOMES UNSETTLING]

114
00:06:02,987 --> 00:06:06,365
Didn't I tell you to stay away
from my daughter and grandson?!

115
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:07,825
- [JORDAN] Grandpa!
- [THUD]

116
00:06:08,493 --> 00:06:11,037
Grandpa, relax. Calm down.

117
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,955
It's okay. It's not him.

118
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:15,333
[JORDAN] Nurse, please
take him to his room.

119
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:19,545
I am so sorry.

120
00:06:20,129 --> 00:06:22,840
Billy, did the caller contact you again?

121
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:24,717
I blocked the number, Auntie Pres.

122
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:26,302
Are you sure that will do?

123
00:06:26,385 --> 00:06:28,805
What if he finds another way
to call you again?

124
00:06:28,888 --> 00:06:30,223
Then I'll block it too.

125
00:06:30,306 --> 00:06:32,725
If you want, you can give me the number.

126
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:34,435
I'll talk to that caller.

127
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:36,729
No need, Auntie Pres.

128
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:39,524
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

129
00:06:39,607 --> 00:06:41,192
- Let's go, Billy!
- Okay.

130
00:06:41,275 --> 00:06:43,694
Auntie, you're not really coming with us?

131
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:45,321
I still have a lot to do here.

132
00:06:45,404 --> 00:06:47,198
- You two have fun, okay?
- Okay.

133
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:48,991
- Ready? Kiss Auntie Pres goodbye.
- Let's go.

134
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:50,493
- Bye.
- Hmm.

135
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:52,453
- Enjoy, enjoy, enjoy.
- Bye, Auntie Pres.

136
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:54,413
- Okay. Bye.
- Bye.

137
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:56,541
Mwah. Hmm?

138
00:06:56,624 --> 00:06:58,960
Mm-hmm. Bye!

139
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:03,047
Bro, I'm sorry about what happened.

140
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:05,341
Please be patient with Grandpa.

141
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:09,720
I'm new here and I guess

142
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:12,181
Grandpa Jude didn't recognize me.

143
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:15,560
The thing is…

144
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:21,274
you and my dad are both bald.

145
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:23,484
They're not on good terms,

146
00:07:24,193 --> 00:07:25,987
so seeing you must have triggered him.

147
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:28,739
Patients with Alzheimer's disease

148
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:33,411
tend to forget
their recent memories first.

149
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:40,209
But they find it hard to forget
deep emotional memories.

150
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:41,669
[EXHALES LOUDLY]

151
00:07:41,752 --> 00:07:46,924
Perhaps you should avoid him for now.

152
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:48,634
- Okay, sir.
- Just to be safe.

153
00:07:48,718 --> 00:07:50,553
Okay, sir.

154
00:07:50,636 --> 00:07:52,346
- Thank you.
- Thank you too.

155
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:59,854
[PHONE RINGING]

156
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:03,941
Hey, dude.

157
00:08:05,276 --> 00:08:07,987
I paid Grandpa a visit,
but I was about to leave.

158
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:14,619
Okay, game. I'll join you guys.

159
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:23,169
[GRUNTS]

160
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:28,466
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:08:28,549 --> 00:08:30,927
[PILLS RATTLING]

162
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:38,017
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

163
00:08:49,195 --> 00:08:54,909
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

164
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:05,503
Billy, can we go there, please?

165
00:09:05,586 --> 00:09:07,088
- Okay, you go first.
- Thank you.

166
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:09,465
- We'll be right behind you. Go, go, go!
- Be careful!

167
00:09:10,091 --> 00:09:11,133
[PHONE CHIMES]

168
00:09:15,721 --> 00:09:17,223
You told her to do this, didn't you?

169
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:19,308
She volunteered.

170
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:21,102
I didn't tell her to.

171
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:22,395
Mm…

172
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,772
That means she still loves you.

173
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:27,233
Think about it.

174
00:09:27,316 --> 00:09:28,651
That's one problem solved.

175
00:09:29,902 --> 00:09:31,279
You're being defensive.

176
00:09:31,362 --> 00:09:32,363
No.

177
00:09:33,197 --> 00:09:37,868
You know, I believe
that Valerie is a good person.

178
00:09:37,952 --> 00:09:40,621
I don't think she has
anything to do with Caloy.

179
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:44,584
Who I'm suing, by the way. Don't forget.

180
00:09:47,628 --> 00:09:49,130
You know, to be honest,

181
00:09:50,464 --> 00:09:53,342
I really got scared when I was in prison.

182
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:56,095
I kept thinking…

183
00:09:57,138 --> 00:09:58,848
About what would happen to your grandpa.

184
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:03,728
How is he?

185
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:06,439
He's okay.

186
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:09,150
He was doing great

187
00:10:10,526 --> 00:10:12,486
until he met the new staff member.

188
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:15,948
The guy looks like my dad.
He's also bald.

189
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:19,118
Grandpa got triggered.

190
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:21,162
So he acted out.

191
00:10:21,662 --> 00:10:22,830
He attacked.

192
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:26,417
I'm sorry, dude.

193
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,589
Just try to understand your grandpa.

194
00:10:33,174 --> 00:10:35,217
It's really hard

195
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:37,678
when you can't escape
the person who hurt you.

196
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:43,059
Are you okay?

197
00:10:44,268 --> 00:10:46,437
Dude. What happened?

198
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:49,273
[CLEARS THROAT]
My father called last night.

199
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:50,608
What did he say?

200
00:10:52,193 --> 00:10:55,071
I didn't listen to what he had to say.
I blocked his number immediately.

201
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:59,075
Auntie Pres said

202
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:01,702
that we should find out
why he was calling.

203
00:11:03,245 --> 00:11:04,288
What for?

204
00:11:05,706 --> 00:11:07,458
There's no point anyway, right?

205
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:09,627
It's your choice.

206
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:14,590
Billy, Bro Dude! Let's check out
the people boxing over there.

207
00:11:14,673 --> 00:11:16,217
- Come on! Let's go!
- [BILLY] I think--

208
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:19,011
Oh, he said he wants to box.
Ask him to go with you.

209
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:20,388
- Go, go, go!
- Come on.

210
00:11:20,471 --> 00:11:22,014
Okay. I'll teach you.

211
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:23,140
[OLIVER] Okay. Look!

212
00:11:23,849 --> 00:11:24,767
Hurry!

213
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:31,315
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

214
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:46,330
[TERE] Unbelievable!

215
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:49,667
Do you think this is your house, huh?

216
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:53,421
If that's so, at least keep it clean!
Look at all this mess!

217
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:55,131
You're treating this place like a bar!

218
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:57,007
- I've been patient with you!
- [ABI] Ms. Tere.

219
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:02,012
I'm sorry. One unit was broken,
so Caloy stayed overtime.

220
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:03,013
[TERE] Overtime?!

221
00:12:03,097 --> 00:12:05,015
Abi, it's written on our contract

222
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:06,976
that this is a computer shop, not a motel.

223
00:12:07,059 --> 00:12:08,561
It's called Click Station for a reason.

224
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:09,937
It's also written on our contract

225
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:13,399
that if you fail to pay rent
for two months, you have to leave.

226
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:15,943
It's been more than that,
and I'm still letting you stay.

227
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:17,987
And this is how you treat my place?!

228
00:12:18,070 --> 00:12:19,572
- Seriously?!
- I know. I know, Ms. Tere!

229
00:12:19,655 --> 00:12:20,656
I know!

230
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:25,411
So I'm going to ask you again
to give us more time.

231
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:26,495
Just a week.

232
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:27,705
A week?

233
00:12:28,289 --> 00:12:29,248
One week.

234
00:12:29,331 --> 00:12:32,334
Okay. If you fail to pay me,
I'm going to do a garage sale,

235
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:33,961
and I'll include all of your things.

236
00:12:34,753 --> 00:12:36,714
- My gosh.
- Sure.

237
00:12:46,724 --> 00:12:48,267
[LOUD THUD]

238
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:54,982
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

239
00:13:01,363 --> 00:13:02,448
Look.

240
00:13:02,531 --> 00:13:04,116
- Watch them.
- Amazing!

241
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:08,704
Wow! Someone's excited.

242
00:13:08,787 --> 00:13:10,789
- Yes.
- Someone's excited!

243
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:13,542
The power comes from the legs.
Just like that.

244
00:13:14,126 --> 00:13:15,461
Let's try it.

245
00:13:15,544 --> 00:13:16,879
- Let's go.
- [BILLY] Go.

246
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:18,297
Show me your moves.

247
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:21,342
- Go, kiddo. Hit him hard.
- Follow what I do.

248
00:13:21,425 --> 00:13:23,219
- Jab, jab.
- Go!

249
00:13:23,302 --> 00:13:24,428
Straight.

250
00:13:25,721 --> 00:13:27,139
Jab, jab, straight.

251
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:28,474
Nice.

252
00:13:28,557 --> 00:13:30,768
- Okay. Nice moves.
- Yes.

253
00:13:30,851 --> 00:13:32,228
Again.

254
00:13:32,311 --> 00:13:33,938
- Jab, jab, straight.
- Jab, jab, straight.

255
00:13:34,021 --> 00:13:36,232
- Pull your feet.
- Oliver, hit him harder!

256
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:37,942
- [OLIVER] Okay.
- [PHONE CHIMES]

257
00:13:38,025 --> 00:13:42,363
CHIEF. LOAN CONCERN. CAN I CALL?

258
00:13:42,446 --> 00:13:44,240
Dude. I just need to make a phone call.

259
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:46,075
- I'll get you some water too.
- [OLIVER] Okay, bye!

260
00:13:46,158 --> 00:13:48,118
- [JORDAN] Sure. Okay.
- Be careful, okay? Careful!

261
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:49,995
Okay. Here's the next thing
that you should do.

262
00:13:51,121 --> 00:13:52,373
Sorry.

263
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:57,419
I'm sorry. If only I had money,
I would've let you borrow it immediately.

264
00:13:58,128 --> 00:14:00,256
It's fine. I expected that anyway.

265
00:14:00,339 --> 00:14:03,175
[CALOY] I got some side hustles.
I'll see if I can earn some, okay?

266
00:14:03,259 --> 00:14:04,677
I want to make it up to you.

267
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:06,303
[BOTTLES CLINK]

268
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:07,471
Hey.

269
00:14:09,473 --> 00:14:12,309
You should take a break from working here.

270
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:15,145
I'm not going to get drunk anymore.
I won't drink here.

271
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:19,358
You really shouldn't be getting drunk.
It's dangerous when you get drunk.

272
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:21,777
Do you know what you called me
last night, huh?

273
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:23,195
- What?
- You called me Bea.

274
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:24,280
- B-Bea?
- Yes.

275
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:26,740
See? You can't remember
because you were wasted.

276
00:14:26,824 --> 00:14:27,825
I've told you this before.

277
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:30,411
Even if it's just the two of us,
get used to calling me Abi!

278
00:14:30,494 --> 00:14:32,413
- Abi! Abi! Abi! Abi! Abi!
- I'm sorry.

279
00:14:32,496 --> 00:14:34,498
Abi, Abi, Abi.

280
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,667
- I'm sorry.
- Get used to calling me Abi.

281
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:39,044
And we shouldn't be seen together.

282
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:42,089
Because your case
with Jordan isn't over yet.

283
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:44,550
- It'll be a big problem.
- [BOTTLES CLINKING]

284
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:45,676
Abi…

285
00:14:47,177 --> 00:14:48,888
Are you firing me?

286
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:52,182
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

287
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:56,103
No, Caloy. I'm not firing you.
What are you saying?

288
00:14:56,186 --> 00:14:58,188
I need you, so why would I fire you?

289
00:14:58,272 --> 00:14:59,690
All I'm saying is--

290
00:14:59,773 --> 00:15:02,318
Stop smiling. I'm being serious here.

291
00:15:02,401 --> 00:15:05,779
All I'm saying is stop coming
to the computer shop!

292
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:07,281
- That's all!
- [SUNGLASSES CLATTER]

293
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,743
What happened to your face?

294
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:15,748
My charge hit me. Tsk!
She's another problem.

295
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:18,584
We really are soulmates.

296
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:22,338
Soulmates, you say?
Want me to rip your soul out?

297
00:15:22,421 --> 00:15:23,464
No, ma'am.

298
00:15:25,549 --> 00:15:26,884
I'm being serious, okay?

299
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:30,346
Use your feet, okay?

300
00:15:30,429 --> 00:15:32,431
Just like this. Ready?

301
00:15:32,514 --> 00:15:33,849
Jab. Jab, straight.

302
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:36,143
- Like that.
- You're good, Bro Dude!

303
00:15:36,226 --> 00:15:37,478
Where did you learn to box?

304
00:15:37,561 --> 00:15:40,814
Grandpa Jude taught me.
He's a great fighter.

305
00:15:41,398 --> 00:15:42,232
Your grandpa?

306
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:46,070
Why did your grandfather teach you
and not your father?

307
00:15:46,153 --> 00:15:47,529
Haven't I told you?

308
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:51,158
My father left me.
It's actually been a while.

309
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:56,038
You didn't try to find him?
You don't know where he is?

310
00:15:57,122 --> 00:15:59,166
- No.
- Why not?

311
00:16:01,418 --> 00:16:04,380
I feel like things are
better off without him.

312
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:07,758
- Try to copy me.
- Okay.

313
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:10,469
Jab! Hook!

314
00:16:10,552 --> 00:16:11,845
Good morning, chief!

315
00:16:11,929 --> 00:16:13,639
Yes, chief.

316
00:16:13,722 --> 00:16:19,395
<i>The bank representative said</i>
<i>the title verification is still ongoing,</i>

317
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:21,105
so they can't release the check yet.

318
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:22,815
- Thanks.
- Okay, got it.

319
00:16:22,898 --> 00:16:24,149
I'll take care of this on Monday.

320
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:25,818
- Thank you, Blaire.
- Are you hungry?

321
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:26,777
Yes.

322
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:28,696
- Want some drinks?
- Two bottles of water, please.

323
00:16:28,779 --> 00:16:30,072
- That'll be 25 each.
- Okay.

324
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:32,992
Here you go, dear.
Let me wipe off your sweat.

325
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:35,202
- [MAN 1] You should rest first.
- [GIRL 1] Mm-hmm.

326
00:16:35,744 --> 00:16:37,579
[MAN 1] You're drenched in sweat!

327
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:40,165
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:41,750
[SELLER] Fifty pesos, miss.

329
00:16:42,626 --> 00:16:44,378
- All right.
- Thank you.

330
00:16:44,461 --> 00:16:46,797
[MAN 1] Play later. Let's eat lunch first.

331
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:47,840
[GIRL 1] Okay.

332
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:49,383
When your mom comes back.

333
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:57,850
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:16:57,933 --> 00:17:02,604
[MUSIC TURNS DRAMATIC]

335
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:04,565
[MUSIC STOPS]

336
00:17:04,648 --> 00:17:11,238
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

337
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:14,867
Dear?

338
00:17:22,583 --> 00:17:24,918
Dear, please hear me out.

339
00:17:25,002 --> 00:17:27,254
I know I did you wrong,

340
00:17:27,337 --> 00:17:29,506
but forgive me, dear!

341
00:17:30,841 --> 00:17:33,635
Dear, let me explain--

342
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:35,137
That's not necessary.

343
00:17:36,805 --> 00:17:38,265
We're fine now.

344
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:42,936
Just leave.

345
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:46,815
Dear, I'm begging you.

346
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:49,026
No, I am begging you.

347
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:55,908
Let this be the last time
we see each other.

348
00:17:55,991 --> 00:17:59,912
[BILLY SNIFFLES, BREATHES SHAKILY]

349
00:18:00,537 --> 00:18:05,584
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

350
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:09,505
[MAN 2] Dear!

351
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:15,469
- [GIRL 2] The fish is ready!
- [BOY 1] Let's eat!

352
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:17,638
- [BOY 2] Hurry up.
- [MAN 2] Okay, okay.

353
00:18:19,431 --> 00:18:24,269
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

354
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:27,189
[WOMAN] Wow!

355
00:18:31,777 --> 00:18:34,279
[CELL PHONE RINGS]

356
00:18:34,905 --> 00:18:36,824
- Hello?
- Hello? [SNIFFLES]

357
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:38,700
Oliver's still with you, right?

358
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:40,410
Uh, yes.

359
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:42,496
- Wait here.
- Okay.

360
00:18:44,748 --> 00:18:45,958
What's wrong?

361
00:18:46,041 --> 00:18:46,959
Are you okay?

362
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:48,460
Keep an eye on him. Please.

363
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:49,962
I'm on my way back.

364
00:18:50,045 --> 00:18:52,381
Dude, what happened?

365
00:18:53,173 --> 00:18:55,092
Jordan, my father is here.

366
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:58,512
[SNIFFLES] Let's go home. Please?

367
00:18:58,595 --> 00:18:59,805
What?

368
00:18:59,888 --> 00:19:01,640
Too bad you have to attend
an online meeting.

369
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:04,017
I didn't get to show you
what Bro Dude taught me.

370
00:19:04,101 --> 00:19:05,811
[BILLY] I'm sorry. I'll make it up to you.

371
00:19:05,894 --> 00:19:07,229
- Show me later.
- [CAR DOOR CLOSES]

372
00:19:08,188 --> 00:19:10,899
- Okay.
- Hey, are you okay?

373
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:11,984
[SNIFFLES]

374
00:19:12,067 --> 00:19:14,236
[SIGHS SHAKILY]

375
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:16,321
You think he's still here?

376
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:17,614
[SNIFFLES]

377
00:19:18,907 --> 00:19:20,117
Okay.

378
00:19:20,993 --> 00:19:22,411
I'll drive you home.

379
00:19:22,494 --> 00:19:23,912
I'll just come back for my bike later.

380
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:26,582
No. [SNIFFLES] I can drive.

381
00:19:26,665 --> 00:19:29,543
- We'll go straight home.
- I know you're not okay.

382
00:19:30,169 --> 00:19:31,545
[SNIFFLES]

383
00:19:31,628 --> 00:19:33,005
Come on, dude.

384
00:19:33,088 --> 00:19:35,090
Let me drive you home.

385
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:36,508
- [SHAKILY] Okay.
- Okay?

386
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:38,260
- Okay. [SNIFFLES]
- Let's go.

387
00:19:46,685 --> 00:19:50,939
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

388
00:19:51,023 --> 00:19:55,319
<i>I wish we could visit</i>
<i>Papa's grave in America.</i>

389
00:19:58,155 --> 00:20:04,661
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

390
00:20:13,712 --> 00:20:14,963
[MUSIC FADES]

391
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:19,593
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

392
00:20:22,512 --> 00:20:24,890
[CAR DOORS CLOSING]

393
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:29,019
- Hey.
- Hi, Auntie Pres.

394
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:32,272
- Did you have fun?
- Yes! Let's do that again!

395
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:34,608
- Sure! Good night, kid.
- [OLIVER] Good night!

396
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:48,413
Dude.

397
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:52,459
You know you can talk to me.

398
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:54,962
Anytime, okay?

399
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:59,716
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

400
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,301
[WHISPERS] Thank you.

401
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:10,060
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

402
00:21:10,143 --> 00:21:12,229
[GATE CLINKS]

403
00:21:12,938 --> 00:21:15,983
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

404
00:21:20,445 --> 00:21:24,574
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING, THEN FADES]

405
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,003
Auntie Pres, I'll drop Oliver off
at school tomorrow, okay?

406
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:45,721
[BAG THUDS]

407
00:21:49,516 --> 00:21:53,186
Jordan already told me what happened.

408
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:54,771
[BILLY SNIFFLES]

409
00:21:56,606 --> 00:21:59,776
You want to talk about it?
I'm here for you.

410
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:09,661
[PRECIOUS SNIFFLES]

411
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:16,460
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

412
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:21,256
[SNIFFLES]

413
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:22,632
Billy…

414
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:28,388
You know, when I first met you,
I was so impressed.

415
00:22:30,474 --> 00:22:34,311
I thought, what an amazing kid you are.

416
00:22:35,312 --> 00:22:38,982
I saw how hard you fought
for Oliver back then.

417
00:22:39,066 --> 00:22:43,528
I realized just how deeply you loved him.

418
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:46,281
[BREATHES SHAKILY]

419
00:22:46,364 --> 00:22:51,078
Even with all the kids
I've cared for at the center,

420
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:56,708
you made me realize
I wanted to be a mother.

421
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:02,339
So if it's okay with you,

422
00:23:02,422 --> 00:23:05,634
let me be a mother to you just this once.

423
00:23:05,717 --> 00:23:06,968
Is that all right?

424
00:23:10,972 --> 00:23:12,474
Is that okay with you, Billy?

425
00:23:14,226 --> 00:23:15,477
[PRECIOUS SNIFFLES]

426
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:22,567
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

427
00:23:22,651 --> 00:23:24,778
Why'd he even come back?

428
00:23:26,404 --> 00:23:29,157
We were doing fine,
weren't we, Auntie Pres?

429
00:23:29,241 --> 00:23:30,742
We were doing just fine.

430
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:32,828
Why's he showing up again?

431
00:23:32,911 --> 00:23:34,996
He's ruining everything.

432
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:37,040
We were doing fine.

433
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:41,586
<i>Mister, please buy something. Mister…</i>

434
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:44,798
<i>- Miss! Miss, please buy--</i>
<i>- Benilda?</i>

435
00:23:44,881 --> 00:23:47,175
- [PANICKED BREATHING]
<i>- Benilda, wait! Hold on.</i>

436
00:23:47,968 --> 00:23:50,178
<i>I won't let you take me away again!</i>

437
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:55,225
<i>I won't let you separate</i>
<i>my brother and me!</i>

438
00:23:56,476 --> 00:23:58,979
<i>But it's for Oliver's own good.</i>

439
00:23:59,062 --> 00:24:02,399
<i>For his own good?</i>
<i>When you're tearing us apart?</i>

440
00:24:04,067 --> 00:24:05,652
<i>Family…</i>

441
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,989
<i>is never meant to be split up.</i>

442
00:24:11,032 --> 00:24:12,742
<i>No one gets left behind.</i>

443
00:24:12,826 --> 00:24:15,453
<i>But you're still not able</i>
<i>to take care of him yourself--</i>

444
00:24:15,537 --> 00:24:16,580
<i>I can do it.</i>

445
00:24:17,164 --> 00:24:19,374
<i>Yes, I can.</i>

446
00:24:19,457 --> 00:24:21,543
<i>Just come with me, please.</i>

447
00:24:21,626 --> 00:24:25,672
<i>Even if you take me again,</i>
<i>I'll run away with my brother.</i>

448
00:24:26,673 --> 00:24:31,553
<i>No matter what you do,</i>
<i>I'll never leave his side.</i>

449
00:24:31,636 --> 00:24:33,513
<i>I won't let anything happen to him.</i>

450
00:24:33,597 --> 00:24:35,348
<i>I understand.</i>

451
00:24:36,224 --> 00:24:37,601
<i>Believe me.</i>

452
00:24:37,684 --> 00:24:44,524
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

453
00:24:53,450 --> 00:24:59,039
[BOTH SNIFFLING, SOBBING SOFTLY]

454
00:24:59,122 --> 00:25:05,879
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

455
00:25:05,962 --> 00:25:12,594
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

456
00:25:23,772 --> 00:25:25,148
<i>Are you going to sue him?</i>

457
00:25:25,232 --> 00:25:26,983
<i>If he won't stay away from me</i>
<i>and my brother.</i>

458
00:25:27,067 --> 00:25:28,652
<i>You've got some nerve, huh?!</i>

459
00:25:29,402 --> 00:25:30,445
<i>That's enough!</i>

460
00:25:31,863 --> 00:25:33,782
<i>When are you meeting</i>
<i>Caloy again?</i>

461
00:25:33,865 --> 00:25:35,742
<i>Next week. The subpoena</i>
<i>has already been issued.</i>

462
00:25:35,825 --> 00:25:37,994
<i>See? You had him locked up.</i>
<i>He won't leave you alone.</i>

463
00:25:38,078 --> 00:25:40,580
<i>He might dig up</i>
<i>more information about you.</i>

464
00:25:40,664 --> 00:25:43,208
<i>I really do need extra work right now.</i>

465
00:25:43,291 --> 00:25:46,962
<i>If an opening comes up</i>
<i>at LoveList, I'll let you know.</i>

466
00:25:47,045 --> 00:25:49,756
<i>We have to be a hundred steps ahead.</i>

467
00:25:49,839 --> 00:25:51,716
<i>You're exactly what I want.</i>

468
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:54,970
<i>The new canteen manager</i>
<i>stood up for me.</i>

469
00:25:55,053 --> 00:25:56,763
<i>- I'll drop you off.</i>
<i>- Oh…</i>

470
00:25:59,224 --> 00:26:01,851
<i>Do you really believe</i>
<i>what you said earlier?</i>

471
00:26:01,935 --> 00:26:03,687
<i>Second chances</i>
<i>can be earned?</i>

472
00:26:03,770 --> 00:26:05,188
<i>About your dad.</i>

473
00:26:05,272 --> 00:26:08,441
<i>And you… do you think</i>
<i>you can forgive?</i>
